window.FTA_TOUR = {"slug":"bach-hopkins","title":"Prelude in C","artist":"Jon Hopkins","bpm":125,"key":"C major","seconds":81.72,"group":"bach","how":"Bach's Prelude in C on felt piano, every note, under Hopkins's machinery: a crunchy kick the whole mix breathes around, a 16th-note bass whose filter opens over minutes, crackle, and a swell into release.","trick":"The swell is Bach's: his eight-bar G pedal (bars 24-31) is where the kick leaves and the Shepard tone climbs, and his bar 32 is where it lands.","stops":[{"t":0,"label":"Bach on felt piano","text":"The Prelude alone on a felt piano, with a few glitches ticking."},{"t":7.68,"label":"The pulse","text":"The pulse: the kick enters and a 16th-note bass follows Bach's lowest note in every bar."},{"t":30.72,"label":"Pad and clap","text":"A pad and a clap; the bass filter keeps opening."},{"t":46.08,"label":"The G pedal swell","text":"Bach's G pedal: the kick leaves, a Shepard tone climbs, then the kick returns in quarters and eighths."},{"t":59.52,"label":"Release","text":"Release on Bach's bar 32. His last four bars loop twice with the breath at -8 dB."},{"t":74.88,"label":"The last chord","text":"The final C chord rings out."}],"checks":{"lufs":-14.0,"tp":-1.6,"clicks":0,"sha":"619B1B63766BE494"},"gram":{"rows":72,"cols":817,"lo":"C1","fps":10,"b64":""}};
